{"name":"Forbidden Forest","hex":"#215354","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"forbidden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Not allowed; specifically disallowed."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["past participle of forbid"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forbidden"},{"term":"forest","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dense uncultivated tract of trees and undergrowth, larger than woods.","Any dense collection or amount."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover an area with trees."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forest"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hogwarts","blocks":[{"text":"Hogwarts School of Witchcraft and Wizardry is a fictional boarding school of magic in the Harry Potter series by J. K. Rowling. It is the primary setting for the first six novels and films and also serves as a major setting in the larger Wizarding World media franchise."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Studio_model_of_Hogwarts_at_Leavesden_Studios.jpg/330px-Studio_model_of_Hogwarts_at_Leavesden_Studios.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hogwarts"},{"title":"The Forbidden Forest","blocks":[{"text":"The Forbidden Forest is a 1955 novel by the Romanian writer Mircea Eliade. The story takes place between 1936 and 1948 in Bucharest and several other European cities, and follows a Romanian man who is on a spiritual quest while being torn between two women. The book was written between the years 1949 and 1954. It contains several elements and themes which also appear in the author's scholarly work, such as initiation rites and the division between sacred and profane time."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0c/Foret_interdite_by_Mircea_Eliade.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Forbidden_Forest"},{"title":"Forbidden Forest (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Forbidden Forest is a game designed by Paul Norman, published by Cosmi Corporation in 1983 for the Commodore 64 and Atari 8-bit computers."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/eb/Forbidden_Forest_%28video_game_box_art%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forbidden_Forest_(video_game)"},{"title":"Forest","blocks":[{"text":"A forest is an ecosystem characterized by a dense community of trees. Hundreds of definitions of forest are used throughout the world, incorporating factors such as tree density, tree height, land use, legal standing, and ecological function. The United Nations' Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO) defines a forest as, \"Land spanning more than 0.5 hectares with trees higher than 5 meters and a canopy cover of more than 10 percent, or trees able to reach these thresholds in situ. It does not include land that is predominantly under agricultural or urban use.\" Using this definition, Global Forest Resources Assessment 2025 found that forests covered 4.14 billion hectares, or approximately 31 percent of the world's land area in 2025."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Aerial_view_of_the_Amazon_Rainforest.jpg/330px-Aerial_view_of_the_Amazon_Rainforest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forest"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Universal-Islands-of-Adventure-Harry-Potter-Castle-9182.jpg/500px-Universal-Islands-of-Adventure-Harry-Potter-Castle-9182.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Universal-Islands-of-Adventure-Harry-Potter-Castle-9182.jpg/1280px-Universal-Islands-of-Adventure-Harry-Potter-Castle-9182.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=